# The incompatible changes of the Go client which are intended against one
# release, like removing or renaming API, which CRI-O adapts to when it bumps
# the module. The first line which is no comment is the tag of that release,
# the others are lines of the "## incompatible changes" section of the report
# of gorelease. make verify-go-api prints the whole report and fails as usual,
# unless it compares with that tag, gorelease found no errors or diagnostics
# and every incompatible change it reports is one of the lines below. Once the
# next release got tagged, gorelease compares with that one, the file is a
# no-op then and gets deleted afterwards, see release.md, which also tells
# when a patch release needs the tag below replaced.
